Template: one phase handoff — `{{docs_dir}}/handoffs/<Wave>-<nn>-<phase>.md` (nn = 01, 02 … within the wave, the next
free number; phase ∈ a b c d e). The main session writes it at the close of EVERY phase session, before the final
message, and ends that session with the exact line `HANDOFF: <path>`. It is the only state the next phase session reads.
- Keep the header labels exactly as written: hooks stamp `- **Main thread:**` (leave it empty) and status-digest
  parses the others. Result ∈ done | partial | fail · Next phase ∈ a | b | c | d | e | none.
- `Next prompt:` is the FIRST line of the next phase's §7 prompt, verbatim (none → `none`).
- ≤ 40 lines, no file contents, no URLs. Side tasks that surface mid-phase go under Notes and are done at the close. The logbook notes feed the doc-sync sheet of phase d (and e).
-->
